        "notes": "Heat from Io's volcanoes at 4.8 µm, our own reduction of 34 Juno JIRAM frames from orbits 41, 43, 47 and 49 (April 2022 to March 2023), the orbits Mura et al. (2024) mapped. Only the night side is kept, where no sunlight is reflected. Each hot spot's total output agrees with the paper's; its peak is lower, because we do not sharpen the images as they do. Color follows the linear scale of their Figure 2. Gray grid: never seen at night in these orbits, including the south and Loki Patera.",
